From 8707ab7423f890e460471ac4a754486244ca0992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrianProk <Prokopczyk.Adrian@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:46:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] 3DS: Show a startup screen with a progress bar
 (MAUSJAGD_PORT)

Game detection and engine start block the main thread for a few
seconds without drawing a frame. The standalone build now shows a
title and a progress bar on the top screen from the end of
initBackend() until the engine has set its resolution and draws its
first frame. The bar advances when the detection starts and when the
engine starts (engineInit()). A ScummVM dialog, e.g. an error message,
ends the startup screen so that it can be seen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 backends/platform/3ds/osystem-graphics.cpp | 89 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 backends/platform/3ds/osystem.cpp          |  8 ++
 backends/platform/3ds/osystem.h            | 21 +++++
 3 files changed, 118 insertions(+)

diff --git a/backends/platform/3ds/osystem-graphics.cpp b/backends/platform/3ds/osystem-graphics.cpp
